Headlines
================================================================================
1. FULL COVARIANCE WAS THE FIX for Lorenz63, not training.
   Switching from diagonal EBIF twist (yesterday) to EKF-init FULL-COV
   twist (today, NO training) jumps from 16.4x -> 55.5x at K=2048 and
   drops DEER iters/window from 16 to 12.

2. Training the twist via Adam on the no-resampling ELBO REGRESSES
   the parallel deployment. neg-ELBO improves (training does its job)
   but DEER iters explode (58 at K=64) and then DEER diverges
   outright at K>=256 (max|par-seq|=1e8, hit MAX_ITER=200).

3. Diagnosis: the learned twist sharpens the proposal, making the
   effective per-step Jacobian stiffer / pushing its spectrum into
   complex eigenvalues that the diagonal Hutchinson Jacobian
   estimator in qdeer.seq1d cannot resolve. This matches the
   feedback memory feedback_deer_damp_complex_eigvals.md:
     Learned twist eff-Jacobian can have complex eigvals;
     drop Schur basis + damp=0.95
   The existing TwistedParallelParticleFilter Lorenz demo deploys
   the same learned twist with Schur basis rotation + damp=0.95
   for exactly this reason; I omitted both in the prototype.

4. Next step: add basis (Schur) and damp_factor passthrough to
   TwistedGumbelParticleFilter.run_parallel, retry K-sweep on the
   learned twist. Expect speedup with learned twist to match or beat
   the EKF baseline once the stiffness is handled.
